# TechTuxAcademy — Cloudflare Pages frontend environment variables.
#
# These are read at build time by Vite (import.meta.env.VITE_<KEY>).
# Set real values in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard under
# Settings → Environment variables — never commit production values.
#
# NOTE: No secrets go here. The frontend authenticates with an httpOnly
# session cookie and a CSRF cookie; there are no API tokens to expose.

# OPTIONAL. Leave this unset in the recommended deployment.
#
# The client defaults to the relative base `/api`. The Cloudflare Pages
# Functions proxy in `functions/api` forwards `/api/*` to the Render service,
# so the SPA works on techtuxacademy.online, www, and *.pages.dev without a
# build-time host — and cookies stay first-party.
#
# Only set this if you bypass the proxy and call the API cross-site. The client
# appends `/api` automatically, so a value without the suffix is fine.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.techtuxacademy.online
